      <div type="clause" n="16">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 16</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>Li ercevesque averad de forfeiture XL sol. en Merchenelahe e li eveske XX sol. e li queo<hi rend="italic">n</hi>s<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.2"/> XX sol. e li barun X sol. e li socheman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.h"/> XL den.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>Li arcevesqe averad de forfaiture<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.30"/> XL solz en Merchenlae e lui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.31"/> evesqes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.32"/> XX solz e lui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.31"/> quenz XX solz e le baroun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.33"/> X solz e li<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.34"/> vilain XL den.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.35"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>De forisfacturis. Archiepiscopus habebit de forisfactura in Merchenelahe XL sol., episcopus XX sol., comes XX sol., baro X sol., uillanus XL denar.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="16" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="260" ed="#robertson"/>Li ercevesque averad de forfeiture XL sol. en Merchenelahe, e li eveske XX sol., e li queons XX sol., e li barun X sol., e li socheman XL den.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>16. Der Erzbischof<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de.1"/> soll an Busse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de1.e"/> 40 Schilling [2 £<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de1.f"/>] erhalten, im Mercier-Rechtsgebiet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de.2"/>, und der Bischof<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de.3"/> 20 Schilling und der Graf 20 Schilling und der Baron 10 Schilling [1/2 £<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de1.f"/>] und der Ceorl (Socman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_16.lnote.de.4"/> <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) 40 Pfennig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">16. The archbishop shall receive as compensation 40 shillings [2 £], in the Mercian legal district, and the bishop 20 shillings and the count 20 shillings and the baron 10 shillings [1/2 £] and the ceorl (socman <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) 40 pennies.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="261" ed="#robertson"/>The archbishop shall have as compensation [for breach of his protection] 40 shillings in the province of Mercia, a bishop 20 shillings, an earl 20 shillings, a baron 10 shillings, and a sokeman 40 pence.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="503">ECf 12.5; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_18-1">Leis Wl 18.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. ECf. 12, 5 | vgl. u. 18, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_18-1">Leis Wl 18.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 260–261 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 502–503, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">der</hi> Villan, <hi rend="italic">von dem wohl, mit IL, das Orig. sprach, war im</hi> 12. <hi rend="italic">Jh. so gesunken, dass Hk um</hi> 1230 <hi rend="italic">einen höheren Stand einsetzte</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the villein, of whom the orig. probably spoke, as IL do, had sunk so low by the 12th cent. that Hk, c. 1230, substituted a higher rank</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">queōs <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">queōs <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forfat. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forfat. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">euestres <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">euestres <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">baron <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">baron <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">le <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">le Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d. <hi rend="italic">abgekürzt, was ich ferner nicht notire, Im;</hi> denir <hi rend="italic">Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d. abbreviated, which I do not note hereafter, Im; denir Isp</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.de1.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">503</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">für Bruch des von ihm verliehenen Schutzes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for breach of the protection granted by him</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.de1.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">503</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hier meint Verf. nicht alte kleine Schillinge; sonst stände Baron und Villan</hi> (10 Schill. Mercisch) <hi rend="italic">gleich</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">here the author does not mean the old small shillings; otherwise baron and villein (10 shill. Mercian) would be equal</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Schutz 5. a. 8b. 11a. e. f. 15b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Schutz 5. a. 8b. 11a. e. f. 15b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Kent und Wessex weichen ab; <hi rend="italic">ebd</hi>.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Kent and Wessex differ; <hi rend="italic">ibid</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Verhältnis 4 : 2 : 1 auch Hn 35, 1 = 87, 5. ECf 12, 5; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Stand 20a. 21e. f. y; Thegn 17d. e; Adel 33</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The ratio 4 : 2 : 1 also in Hn 35, 1 = 87, 5. ECf 12, 5; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Stand 20a. 21e. f. y; Thegn 17d. e; Adel 33</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_16.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Socman 1a. 2. 3; Bauer 4b. 8a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Socman 1a. 2. 3; Bauer 4b. 8a</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
